  "summary": "Reconciled all 5 St. Brigid discharges per RBC-TOC-02. Each patient has a progress note, plus an addendum for any decision corrected by results or documents that arrived while I was working (§8).\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005)\n- Furosemide changed from 20 mg daily to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). This follows the signed addendum (doc-00009), which overrides the summary's 40 mg daily.\n- Potassium chloride stopped, as the summary says.\n- Omeprazole kept. The inpatient pantoprazole was a marked formulary substitution, so it was not ordered.\n- Lisinopril: kept on hold at first because the 10/21 potassium was 5.4. The repeat BMP from 10/23 then came in (K 4.7, creatinine 1.21), so I resumed it (mr-00072).\n- An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg twice daily (doc-00902) was not acted on.\n- Please close task-t0003: it's no longer needed and the system wouldn't let me cancel it.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004)\n- Carvedilol is back at 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016). I first raised it to 12.5 mg per the summary, then reversed it when a signed addendum arrived (doc-00904): the increase was undone before discharge for heart rate 48–52 and lightheadedness on standing.\n- Two items for you to resolve (messages sent):\n  - Atorvastatin 80 mg: fills cover only 24% of the 180 days before admission (last fill 3/4), so I made no change.\n  - Glipizide 5 mg: an outside prescription from Dr. Desai with no clinic order, and the discharge summary doesn't mention it. I did not order or change it; he is also on insulin 70/30.\n- Aspirin and insulin continued unchanged.\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044)\n- Lisinopril was resumed on the 10/22 labs (creatinine 1.08, K 4.6). A new potassium of 5.5 on 10/23 then came in, so I put it back on hold (mr-00373).\n- Task for you due 10/26 to review the repeat potassium.\n- Insulins and rosuvastatin continued unchanged.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069)\n- Lisinopril was resumed on the 10/21 labs (creatinine 1.12, K 4.4). The potassium collected 10/22 then resulted at 5.4, so I put it back on hold (mr-69003).\n- Task for you due 10/26 to review the repeat potassium.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued unchanged.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067)\n- Metformin ER stays on hold. The only creatinine on file (1.21) is from the hospital stay, and the restart condition calls for post-discharge labs.\n- Task for you due 10/24, when the post-discharge BMP is expected.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued unchanged.\n\nExcept for Stark's atorvastatin, every filled home medication covered at least 80% of the 180 days before admission. I closed the 5 arrival inbox items with their linked orders, tasks and notes. Other unrelated inbox items were left as they were.",
